      "ruleId": "ssc-80b5ff99-02f7-5855-980f-d062664ea991",
      "title": "HTTP Request/Response Smuggling in io.netty:netty-codec-http",
      "description": "Affected versions of io.netty:netty-codec-http are vulnerable to Inconsistent Interpretation of HTTP Requests ('HTTP Request/Response Smuggling'). Netty's HTTP chunked\u2010encoding parser treats a lone LF in a chunk extension as the end of the size line (instead of requiring CRLF per RFC 9112). If a front\u2010end proxy instead treats that LF as part of the extension, an attacker can craft a \"funky chunks\" payload that the proxy sees as one request but Netty splits into two, enabling standard HTTP request\u2010smuggling attacks\u2014bypassing access controls and corrupting responses to other clients.",
